# pins of the sound check built from the OFFICIAL Lean v4.37.0-rc1 sources (used with
# `check-sound.sh --pins <this file>`; the 4.36 pins.env stays the default). Same format as pins.env: PIN <name> <sha256> <path>
# (paths node-local under /scratch; copy there with tools/deploy.sh), enforced on every run, re-hashed at the end.
# TC36=@components = config/components.json lean_toolchains["leanprover/lean4:v4.37.0-rc1"].prefix (tools/addrelease.py 4.37.0-rc1;
# a shared ~/.elan); a verified node-local copy also works, e.g. /scratch/fastverify-next/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.37.0-rc1.
SOUND_VERSION=sound-437-v2 (sound check for Lean v4.37.0-rc1, check-sound v2.2 wiring [--hide]: ccmp e046aa89 = the official v4.37.0-rc1 lake-comparator judge code [Lake/CLI/Check.lean 0b77e129 + concurrency changes] linked against the official 4.37.0-rc1 libraries [Lake.Check.Compare/Axioms = the 4.37 judge, incl. the rule 'Challenge definition is not sorried']; pleanchecker acf82e83 = parallel Lean.Replay ported to the 4.37 API [Lean.Replay order changes, #15853] + the veto-only export-record check (every export record whose name the final kernel environment contains must equal the kernel constant; quot records canonical; closes Lean #15100/#15101-class single-kernel bypasses) + kernel-generated inductive constants only + the encapsulated two-environment replay driven by the untrusted hide list of --hide, each attempt under its own cancel token with a time budget [PCHK_ENCAP_BUDGET_MS, default 600 s] after which the full environment decides; `lake build` with the official 4.37.0-rc1 toolchain = linked against the release's official 4.37 kernel libraries libleancpp.a/libleanrt.a [S1(4): released kernel library; includes the #16489 fix]; gruszka ece04e74 = the independent second kernel (portable reproducible build, tools/reproduce/portable-gruszka.sh); con_leche 8fff3f05 and nanoda 5c34d612 = optional veto-only extra kernels bundled with the official v4.37.0-rc1 release; details: check/sound/README.md)
TC_VERSION=leanprover/lean4:v4.37.0-rc1
TC_LABEL=4.37.0-rc1
TC36=@components
PIN ccmp e046aa895f20d9a2edd127e07264d10d5a330c178ff4b2a3308f0cd21c217ddd /scratch/fastverify-next/sound/e046aa89/ccmp
PIN pleanchecker acf82e8321cbfebc53a6fbadc4f2f6fc535a44b7eb6468431abf4af995993135 /scratch/fastverify-next/sound/acf82e83/pleanchecker
PIN gruszka ece04e7458efafd34e71330e982bf3b46904d48ff5f1089c7094844c9562fe58 /scratch/fastverify-next/gruszka/ece04e74/gruszka
PIN selftest_comparator 9c77b8d2c3c5fb92a8681e5f9d9d9bde0a8ff0fe35ecc5a31ac3024ff4f12802 /scratch/fastverify-next/selftest/comparator.json
PIN selftest_challenge f83cfdd3029814bd61d88e808b2c2e33344ca893214cfec0faa15c66c1048af0 /scratch/fastverify-next/selftest/challenge.export
PIN selftest_good cbc6a26ce8c2c9b4e97085d6822c33026eb36e15ba24a5be0ec8f25746e4d281 /scratch/fastverify-next/selftest/good.export
PIN selftest_bad a48f2d1c4c8e6d5b4be291f72a64926c9afa8398508e02fb68cec2df73a0513f /scratch/fastverify-next/selftest/bad.export
# v2.3-H: extra VETO-ONLY kernels of check-sound(-svc).sh = the binaries BUNDLED with the official
# Lean v4.37.0-rc1 release (toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.37.0-rc1.json bin/con-leche, bin/nanoda_bin; release archive
# sha256 2e1bbb83..., commit 0b77e129), copied unchanged; selftest_kbad = selftest_good with the proof of fvSelfTest made
# ill-typed (check/sound/test/run.sh's kernel-bad mutant). Optional lines: without them the judge is v2.2's two-kernel judge.
PIN con_leche 8fff3f055d032b66d5262cb6db4fb916328b4931a98634630f7481b1e3449308 /scratch/fastverify-next/extra-kernels/8fff3f05/con-leche
PIN nanoda 5c34d6124b19dfd23c7d0377b520893cf8adec5c23fa0c809dde9e38eb201ffe /scratch/fastverify-next/extra-kernels/5c34d612/nanoda_bin
PIN selftest_kbad 2a3d286b326a1051de0f04609157c80efa767258afa5553904cf85d219639dfe /scratch/fastverify-next/selftest/selftest-kbad.export
